A||||9||Old Lar||Archie's Show||||1||
Z||000000||Old Lar||04-21-2001||10:52 PM||||Who went to Archie's?  Lets have a report of whaaattts suuuppp.||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT GT 87||04-22-2001||02:39 PM||||Well I went. Many people that were there had come to this yearly event before. But this was my first time. It was FANTASTIC  !! Archie had several cars to take rides in as did many of the people that came with their V-8's.  I had a great ride in a rebodied car, I think it was the Fino, it "just" had 270 H.P.!!!!!!!!!  The quality is first rate on these rebodied cars. The street and hiway out in front of his shop sounded like a race track, the sound of these cars have to be heard to be appreciated!!!!  Oh - I forgot that Archie had a great lunch for everyone also.  I am a new member of NIFE, it is a great club .      Steve       P.S. I took some great pictures , but sorry they are not digital||||reg||1
Z||000002||DL10||04-22-2001||03:57 PM||||It was my first trip to Archie's and one of his V8 seminars. I had a great time and learned a lot about what it takes to do a V-8 swap.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DL10 (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||04-22-2001||04:15 PM||||I was there... It was a great day. I learned a little more about that V8 swap the '85s getting soon.. & I meet a few fellow forum members...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||04-22-2001||08:49 PM||||I was really hoping that you guys would tell<BR>me it was a bad show so that I'd feel better<BR>since I didn't go. :~(<BR>DAMN, I knew I should-a went!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||04-23-2001||03:07 AM||||Archie is a great guy.  He took time to talk to me personally and answered the questions I had.<P>You have to own one of these V8 fieros, they are loud and FAST.<P>The rides that archie gave was awesome, I was watching the speedometer and sometimes the needle was moving as quick as the tach.<BR>I noticed that the v8 will reach a high speed very quickly. <P>Im totally on planning to put a v8 in my fiero.  The engine swap looks clean.  It doesn't look tight at all.  The sound of the v8 rumbling is SWEET.<P>Too bad i didn't meet anyone from the forum, maybe archie can have "hello my name is "" name tags next year" with their forum handle underneath.<P>Thanks Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroLT1||04-23-2001||07:38 AM||||I was there. Got to say HI to some old faces and met some new ones. Took a couple of "would be V8'ers" for a quick spin around the block on the LT1. Snaped a few necks in the process.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Had a lot of fun!!! Can't wait for next year's.<P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR> <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||04-23-2001||05:12 PM||||Thank You for the kind words.<P>I would like to thank everyone who attended for making this such a successful event. We had 75+/- attendees.<P>It was a nice sunny afternoon and many ppl brought out their Fieros. Haze brought out his latest 355 Nosed car and it looks even better in person than in the pics.<P>Several others from the Forum brought their cars and they all were lookin good.<P>The NIFE 2001 Raffle car was here and it's a REAL NICE '88 GT with "T's" & low miles, Paul V did a real nice job getting it ready for your viewing. Raffle tickets are available online at the NIFE site or from Paul.<P>These pics were taken while everyone was indoors for the seminar. Before & After the Seminar this area was full of people handing out and V-8 cars parading in & out. We had a new feature this year, giving rides to those who wanted their 1st ride in a V-8 Fiero. According to the un-official count a total of 43 people got a ride in one of several V-8 cars. For a couple of hours it was like an Amusement park ride. With a line of people waiting for rides and cars coming in & out. A car would come in and the right side door would open & someone get out then someone else would jump in and the ride would commence. This was very successful (way over & above my expectations) and we will attempt the same thing at a couple other events this season.<P>I'd have to say my biggest thrill of the day was taking Winstons' LT1 Formula for a test drive. That car will fly, it made me miss my LT1 Chop Top car. I haven't had as much fun driving a Fiero since I sold my Chop Top. I MUST build myself another LT1 car.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-878s.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-881s.jpg"> <P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||KissMySSFiero||04-25-2001||11:21 PM||||well i wish i could have gone.  i decided on goin to fla for the week.  hehe.  i hope i can get to see some v8 cars next month at some shows.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
Z||000009||Archie||04-26-2001||12:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>  i hope i can get to see some v8 cars next month at some shows.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You can see a bunch next weekend (May 5) in Paxton, IL.<P>Archie||||reg||1
